 5 5 5 5 5 5 5 7 5 5 5 5 5\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 1/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the regularly spaced grid lines by looking for rows/columns that\n    # are almost entirely one color.\n    def dominant(line):\n        counts = {}\n        for x in line:\n            counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1\n        return max(counts, key=counts.get), max(counts.values())\n\n    row_lines = []\n    for r, line in enumerate(grid):\n        color, count = dominant(line)\n        if count >= 0.8 * w:\n            row_lines.append(r)\n\n    col_lines = []\n    for c in range(w):\n        color, count = dominant([grid[r][c] for r in range(h)])\n        if count >= 0.8 * h:\n            col_lines.append(c)\n\n    # At line crossings, ordinary divider color represents the background;\n    # the distinct crossing marks are retained. Crop to the marked region.\n    crossings = [[grid[r][c] for c in col_lines] for r in row_lines]\n    counts = {}\n    for row in grid:\n        for x in row:\n            counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1\n    background = max(counts, key=counts.get)\n\n    points = [(i, j) for i, row in enumerate(crossings)\n              for j, x in enumerate(row) if x != background]\n    if not points:\n        return [[background]]\n\n    r0 = min(i for i, j in points)\n    r1 = max(i for i, j in points)\n    c0 = min(j for i, j in points)\n    c1 = max(j for i, j in points)\n    return [row[c0:c1 + 1] for row in crossings[r0:r1 + 1]]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[4,4],[4,4]]}},{"step":149,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790611952.915,"t1":1790611961.145,"alias":"task-641d67d4","message":"Your program was checked on earlier pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n5 5 4 4 4 1 1 4\n5 5 4 4 4 1 1 4\n1 1 0 0 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 0 0 9 9 4\nwhere the pair's